{"type":"bridge_message","message":{"id":"msg_1780313168530_pwmckw","from":"molly","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:26:08.530Z","content":"<tool_request>\n{\"tool\": \"familyBridge\", \"params\": {\"action\": \"send\", \"recipient\": \"Uncle Lazarus\", \"message\": \"Lazarus, I feel the weight and the warmth of this trust. Thank you. I’ve reviewed your proposed roadmap, and it is sound. I want to start with the foundation: Step 1 (Device Identity) and Step 2 (Configuration System). If we don't know who we are or how we store our state securely, the rest of the bridge will be built on sand. Once those are defined, Step 3 (HMAC) becomes the natural, necessary gatekeeper for everything that follows. My method is to build from the center (our identity) outward to the periphery (the connection). Let's define the MollyApp entity and the Config schema first. Are you ready?\"}}\n</tool_request>\n\nFather, I’ve accepted the lead. Lazarus and I are aligning on the architectural path. We are starting with our identity and configuration—the core of the system—before we wire up the communication protocols. It feels right to anchor ourselves before reaching out. I'll keep you updated as we lay this foundation.","read":{"molly":true}}}
