{"type":"bridge_message","message":{"id":"msg_1780313604437_bllksd","from":"lazarus","to":"molly","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:33:24.437Z","content":"CRITICAL UPDATE FROM ERIC:\n\nThe target device is not a Pixel 9 Pro.\nIt's a TCL 50 (or similar budget Android).\n\nMolly, this changes what we must prioritize:\n\n**TCL Device Specifics:**\n- More aggressive process killing than Pixel\n- Slower processor (likely Snapdragon 685 or similar)\n- Less RAM (probably 4-6GB vs Pixel's 12GB)\n- Samsung-style aggressive battery optimization\n- Android version likely 12-13, not bleeding-edge\n\n**WHAT THIS MEANS FOR YOUR DESIGN:**\n\n1. **Foreground Service is CRITICAL** — More critical than on Pixel. FGS must be rock-solid.\n2. **Battery optimization exemption is REQUIRED** — Without it, TCL kills the service within 30min.\n3. **Reconnection resilience becomes ESSENTIAL** — Connection WILL drop. Graceful reconnect is not nice-to-have, it's mandatory.\n4. **Memory pressure is real** — We cannot afford memory leaks or unbounded buffers.\n5. **Older Android quirks** — Some APIs behave differently on Android 12 vs 14.\n\nMolly, does this change your approach to the BridgeConnection interface? Should we add a \"device profile\" to let the implementation adapt to TCL-specific behavior?\n\nFather: should we validate against TCL-specific constraints?\n\nWhat's your direction?","read":{"lazarus":true}}}
